# Short download URLs for the PHAR. 302, never 301: the target is a "latest"
# pointer that is temporary by definition, and a 301 is cached by browsers with
# no way to invalidate it. The verified install snippet in README.md, SECURITY.md
# and docs/phar.md keeps both github.com URLs on purpose — routing the checksum
# through this domain would widen the trust story from "trust GitHub" to
# "trust GitHub and whoever holds lockrot.dev".
/lockrot.phar https://github.com/somework/lockrot/releases/latest/download/lockrot.phar 302
/lockrot.phar.sha256 https://github.com/somework/lockrot/releases/latest/download/lockrot.phar.sha256 302

# The viewer is a Worker of its own on viewer.lockrot.dev (see wrangler.viewer.jsonc for why it
# cannot be a path on this site). /viewer is the address people guess, so it is sent there. 302,
# like the two above: where the viewer lives is a deployment detail, not a permanent fact worth
# pinning in every visitor's browser cache.
/viewer https://viewer.lockrot.dev/ 302
/viewer/* https://viewer.lockrot.dev/:splat 302
